---
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../data/site';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Panel from '../components/Panel.astro';
---
<Site
  title="Services: GTM, audits, training and AI consulting | DNA4Digital"
  description="GTM and process consulting, AI readiness audits, role-based training and implementation. I fix the revenue process first, then automate the parts worth automating."
>
  <Panel rung={0} kicker="01 · Services">
    <h1>Practical AI, with a return you can see</h1>
    <p class="lead">I help companies put AI where it pays back, starting with the revenue process it has to run on. I audit how the work moves, train your team on its own data and build the automations myself.</p>
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#gtm">GTM &amp; processes</a><a href="#delivery">How it's delivered</a><a href="#training">Training</a><a href="#audit">Audits</a><a href="#consulting">Consulting</a>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="gtm">Go-to-market and the processes underneath it</h2>
    <p>GTM is where I do my best work, and where I see the most AI budget wasted. The usual first move is to point AI at the work you can see: drafting emails, summarising calls, generating content. Underneath, each person reads the pipeline stages differently, leads wait four days between marketing and sales, the CRM has three fields for the same thing, and nobody has written down what &ldquo;qualified&rdquo; means.</p>
    <p>Automate that and you get the same confusion at higher speed. I work on both layers, in order: first I make the revenue process clear enough to write down, then I add AI to the steps your team repeats most.</p>
    <div class="pcards">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Revenue process mapping</h3><p>I map the full journey from first touch to closed and renewed: stage definitions, exit criteria, owners, and the handoffs where deals get dropped.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Funnel &amp; pipeline hygiene</h3><p>Qualification rules everyone applies the same way, forecast inputs you can trust, and a CRM trimmed to the fields people use.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>GTM automation</h3><p>Research, enrichment, routing, follow-up, call notes and reporting, built on a process that already works so the time savings last.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Enablement for revenue teams</h3><p>I train SDRs, AEs, marketing and CS on the workflows for their own role, using your data and your current deals.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout"><p><strong>What you get:</strong> a mapped GTM process, the friction points ranked by what they cost you, and a 90-day plan that splits them into &ldquo;fix the process&rdquo; and &ldquo;automate it&rdquo;.</p></div>

    <h2 id="delivery">What happens after the audit</h2>
    <p>Engagements start with an audit, a process map and a ranked list of what's costing you money. The next step depends on what the audit finds.</p>
    <p><strong>If the fix is process and configuration</strong>, I do it myself in a matter of weeks: automations, CRM architecture, SOPs, dashboards, and training your team to run it all without me.</p>
    <p><strong>If the fix needs software built</strong>, I bring in Yameo, a Dutch-Polish software house that has delivered enterprise systems for banking, insurance and healthcare since 2006, on a fixed price, a fixed date and a signed SLA. I'm an Associate Partner there. I stay on the engagement as the person accountable for whether the system solves your problem. You keep working with me throughout, and Yameo only builds what configuration can't do.</p>
    <div class="pcards">
      <div class="pcard">
        <h3>I do this myself (DNA4Digital)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>GTM and revenue process design</li>
          <li>Process mapping, SOPs, KPIs</li>
          <li>AI readiness audits and roadmaps</li>
          <li>Low-code automation (n8n, Zapier, HubSpot)</li>
          <li>Training and enablement</li>
          <li>Dashboards and reporting (Looker Studio)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pcard">
        <h3>I bring in the team (via Yameo)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Custom software and platform builds</li>
          <li>System integrations and migrations at scale</li>
          <li>Regulated-industry work needing compliance sign-off</li>
          <li>Anything needing an engineering team for months</li>
          <li>Fixed-price, fixed-date, SLA-backed delivery</li>
          <li>Long-term embedded development partnership</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout"><p>My rule of thumb: if configuration can do it, I do it. If it needs code, engineers and a signed SLA, Yameo builds it and I stay accountable for the outcome.</p></div>

    <h2 id="training">Training and workshops</h2>
    <p>I build each programme around the roles and processes in your company. Your people practise on their own data and tasks, so they can use AI in their job the same week.</p>
    <div class="pcards three">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Marketing &amp; sales</h3><p>Ready-to-run workflows for funnels, content, research, analytics and CRM work.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Operations &amp; admin</h3><p>Document standards, tidier procedures, quality control and automation.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>HR &amp; knowledge</h3><p>Onboarding, knowledge bases, policies and SOPs that new starters can find and follow.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="audit">Audits</h2>
    <p>I analyse your processes and data to find where AI will pay back first. You get an implementation plan that names, for each step, the number to move, the baseline and the timeframe.</p>
    <p>After the audit workshop you leave with priorities, a process map and tool recommendations.</p>
    <div class="btnrow">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book an audit call</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/ai-readiness/">Take the AI readiness test</a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="consulting">Consulting</h2>
    <p>I implement AI end to end, from the first quick wins to standards your team keeps using: automations, AI assistants, knowledge bases and SOPs, each fitted to how your organisation runs today.</p>
    <div class="pcards three">
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Quick wins</h3><p>ROI mapping and the first automations that give your team its time back.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Assistants &amp; automation</h3><p>Prompt design, usage policies and integrations, built as workflows you can audit.</p></div>
      <div class="pcard"><h3>Knowledge repos &amp; SOPs</h3><p>Standard documents, policies and checklists, kept current and easy to find.</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Start with a 30-minute call</h2>
    <p>The call is free and online. We'll work out whether you should start with an audit, training or consulting.</p>
    <div class="btnrow"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a free consultation</a></div>
  </Panel>
</Site>
